  data: {
    LLM: "1. Starting: The player with the highest double leads (usually the 6-6).\n2. Matching: Players take turns placing a tile so that one end matches an open end of the line of play.\n3. Drawing: In 'Draw' dominoes, if you cannot move, you must draw from the boneyard until a move is possible. In 'Block' dominoes, you simply pass.\n4. Blocking: If no player can move and the boneyard is empty, the game is blocked.",
    Player: "1. Starting: The player with the highest double leads (usually the 6-6).\n2. Matching: Players take turns placing a tile so that one end matches an open end of the line of play.\n3. Drawing: In 'Draw' dominoes, if you cannot move, you must draw from the boneyard until a move is possible. In 'Block' dominoes, you simply pass.\n4. Blocking: If no player can move and the boneyard is empty, the game is blocked.",
    objective: 'Empty your hand of tiles or have the lowest total pip count when the game is blocked.',
    gameplay: "1. Starting: The player with the highest double leads (usually the 6-6).\n2. Matching: Players take turns placing a tile so that one end matches an open end of the line of play.\n3. Drawing: In 'Draw' dominoes, if you cannot move, you must draw from the boneyard until a move is possible. In 'Block' dominoes, you simply pass.\n4. Blocking: If no player can move and the boneyard is empty, the game is blocked.",
    keyRules: [
      'Doubles are usually played crosswise to the line.',
      'The line can grow in two directions (standard) or four (spinners).',
      "A 'Blocked' game winner is the player with the lowest pip total remaining.",
    ],
